{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":74774,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2024,8,6]],"date-time":"2024-08-06T23:02:02Z","timestamp":1722985322065},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Valley International","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["IJMEI"],"DOI":"10.18535\/ijmei\/v1i10.03","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2015,12,20]],"date-time":"2015-12-20T07:23:35Z","timestamp":1450596215000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["IMPACT OF MICROFINANCE ON HOUSEHOLD INCOME: EVIDENCE FROM VILLAGE LEVEL STUDY IN ORISSA"],"prefix":"10.18535","author":[{"name":"Dept of Agricultural Economics, College of Agriculture Bhawanipatna, O.U.A.T, Bhubaneswar, India","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"R.K.","family":"Rout","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"7803","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2015,12,20]]},"container-title":["International Journal of management and economics Invention"],"original-title":["IMPACT OF MICROFINANCE ON HOUSEHOLD INCOME: EVIDENCE FROM VILLAGE LEVEL STUDY IN ORISSA"],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2015,12,20]],"date-time":"2015-12-20T07:23:36Z","timestamp":1450596216000},"score":30.690712,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/rajournals.in\/images\/ijmeiarticle\/v1-i10\/3ijmei.pdf"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2015,12,20]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.18535\/ijmei\/v1i10.03","ISSN":["2395-7220"],"issn-type":[{"type":"electronic","value":"2395-7220"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2015,12,20]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,30]],"date-time":"2026-07-30T11:39:16Z","timestamp":1785411556543,"version":"3.56.0"},"publisher":"Wellcome","award":"221702","DOI":"10.35802\/221702","type":"grant","created":{"date-parts":[[2021,3,12]],"date-time":"2021-03-12T09:27:57Z","timestamp":1615541277000},"source":"Crossref","prefix":"10.35802","member":"13928","project":[{"project-title":[{"title":"Recombinant snakebite antivenom for sub-Saharan Africa"}],"project-description":[{"description":"Sub-Saharan Africa (sSA) is heavily burdened by snakebite envenoming. Existing antivenoms are scarce and many have suboptimal therapeutic properties. To improve snakebite envenoming therapy, the application of carefully designed mixtures of fully human monoclonal immunoglobulin G (IgG) antibodies for systemic and nanobodies for locally acting toxins poses as not only a therapeutically promising, but also scientifically feasible solution. Therefore, taking advantage of our well-established discovery pipelines and expertise in working with oligoclonal and broadly-neutralizing antibodies against toxins, we will develop a broad-spectrum (polyvalent) recombinant antivenom for sSA. The project will focus on the following technical goals that we believe have a potential to deliver measurable societal and humanitarian health impact: 1) The identification and isolation of all medically relevant snake venom toxins that need to be neutralized by a recombinant antivenom for sSA and 2) the discovery of a well-characterized panel of broadly-neutralizing IgGs and nanobodies that can neutralize all medically relevant systemically-acting and deep tissue penetrating toxins found in the 24 medically most relevant snake species from this region. Combined, these efforts will create a substantial shift in snakebite envenoming therapy and will enable the clinical development of improved, low-cost, and quality-assured snakebite therapeutics for victims in sSA.","language":"en"}],"investigator":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2195-0972","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"John","family":"McCafferty","affiliation":[{"name":"IONTAS","country":"GB"}]}],"lead-investigator":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6918-5574","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Andreas","family":"Laustsen","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/04qtj9h94","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Technical University of Denmark","country":"DK"}]}],"award-amount":{"amount":3081450.0,"currency":"GBP"},"award-start":{"date-parts":[[2021,3,1]]},"award-end":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,28]]},"funding":[{"type":"grant","scheme":"Snakebite Priority Area","award-amount":{"amount":3081450.0,"currency":"GBP","percentage":100},"funder":{"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100010269","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Wellcome Trust"}}]}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,23]],"date-time":"2024-01-23T06:17:10Z","timestamp":1705990630000},"score":29.23818,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/europepmc.org\/grantfinder\/grantdetails?query=pi:\"%7BDr%7D%7BMcCafferty%7D%7BJohn%7D%7BJ%7D\" gid:\"221702\" ga:\"Wellcome Trust\""}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2021,3,1]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.35802\/221702"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,24]],"date-time":"2026-10-24T15:52:07Z","timestamp":1792857127248,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":62,"publisher":"MDPI AG","issue":"12","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2018,12,13]],"date-time":"2018-12-13T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1544659200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Toxins"],"abstract":"<jats:p>Snakebite envenoming is a neglected tropical disease that each year claims the lives of 80,000\u2013140,000 victims worldwide. The only effective treatment against envenoming involves intravenous administration of antivenoms that comprise antibodies that have been isolated from the plasma of immunized animals, typically horses. The drawbacks of such conventional horse-derived antivenoms include their propensity for causing allergenic adverse reactions due to their heterologous and foreign nature, an inability to effectively neutralize toxins in distal tissue, a low content of toxin-neutralizing antibodies, and a complex manufacturing process that is dependent on husbandry and procurement of snake venoms. In recent years, an opportunity to develop a fundamentally novel type of antivenom has presented itself. By using modern antibody discovery strategies, such as phage display selection, and repurposing small molecule enzyme inhibitors, next-generation antivenoms that obviate the drawbacks of existing plasma-derived antivenoms could be developed. This article describes the conceptualization of a novel therapeutic development strategy for biosynthetic oligoclonal antivenom (BOA) for snakebites based on recombinantly expressed oligoclonal mixtures of human monoclonal antibodies, possibly combined with repurposed small molecule enzyme inhibitors.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3390\/toxins10120534","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2018,12,14]],"date-time":"2018-12-14T03:58:17Z","timestamp":1544759897000},"page":"534","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3390\/mdpi_crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":97,"title":["Biosynthetic Oligoclonal Antivenom (BOA) for Snakebite and Next-Generation Treatments for Snakebite Victims"],"prefix":"10.3390","volume":"10","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6100-3251","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"R. Manjunatha","family":"Kini","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Biological Sciences, National University of Singapore, 14 Science Drive 4, Singapore 117543, Singapore"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Sachdev S.","family":"Sidhu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Molecular Genetics, The Donnelly Centre, University of Toronto, 160 College Street, Toronto, ON M5S 3E1, Canada"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6918-5574","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Andreas Hougaard","family":"Laustsen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Technical University of Denmark, DK-2800 Kongens Lyngby, Denmark"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"1968","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2018,12,13]]},"reference":[{"key":"ref_1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"38","DOI":"10.1186\/s40409-017-0127-6","article-title":"Snakebite envenomation turns again into a neglected tropical disease!","volume":"23","author":"Chippaux","year":"2017","journal-title":"J. Venom Anim. Toxins Incl. Trop. Dis."},{"key":"ref_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"17063","DOI":"10.1038\/nrdp.2017.63","article-title":"Snakebite envenoming","volume":"3","author":"Calvete","year":"2017","journal-title":"Nat. Rev. Dis. Primers"},{"key":"ref_3","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Mohapatra, B., Warrell, D.A., Suraweera, W., Bhatia, P., Dhingra, N., Jotkar, R.M., Rodriguez, P.S., Mishra, K., Whitaker, R., and Jha, P. (2011). Snakebite mortality in India: A nationally representative mortality survey. PLoS Negl. Trop. Dis., 5.","DOI":"10.1371\/journal.pntd.0001018"},{"key":"ref_4","unstructured":"Meier, J., and White, J. (1995). Clinical toxicology of snakebite in Asia. Handbook of Clinical Toxicology of Animal Venoms and Poisons, CRC Press."},{"key":"ref_5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"5270","DOI":"10.2174\/1381612822666160623073438","article-title":"From Fangs to Pharmacology: The Future of Snakebite Envenoming Therapy","volume":"22","author":"Laustsen","year":"2016","journal-title":"Curr. Pharm. Des."},{"key":"ref_6","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"369","DOI":"10.2174\/187152811797200669","article-title":"Antivenoms for snakebite envenomings","volume":"10","author":"Lomonte","year":"2011","journal-title":"Inflamm. Allergy Drug Targets"},{"key":"ref_7","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"17","DOI":"10.1136\/bmj.292.6512.17","article-title":"Prediction, prevention, and mechanism of early (anaphylactic) antivenom reactions in victims of snake bites","volume":"292","author":"Malasit","year":"1986","journal-title":"Br. Med. J. (Clin. Res. Ed.)"},{"key":"ref_8","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"541","DOI":"10.1016\/S0041-0101(02)00393-8","article-title":"Report of a WHO workshop on the standardization and control of antivenoms","volume":"41","author":"Theakston","year":"2003","journal-title":"Toxicon"},{"key":"ref_9","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"277","DOI":"10.1081\/CLT-120021113","article-title":"Snake antivenoms","volume":"41","author":"Lalloo","year":"2003","journal-title":"J. Toxicol. Clin. Toxicol."},{"key":"ref_10","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"74","DOI":"10.1016\/S0035-9203(01)90339-6","article-title":"An open, randomized comparative trial of two antivenoms for the treatment of envenoming by Sri Lankan Russell\u2019s viper (Daboia russelii russelii)","volume":"95","author":"Ariaratnam","year":"2001","journal-title":"Trans. R. Soc. Trop. Med. Hyg."},{"key":"ref_11","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"200","DOI":"10.1016\/j.annemergmed.2003.08.009","article-title":"Initial experience with Crotalidae polyvalent immune Fab (ovine) antivenom in the treatment of copperhead snakebite","volume":"43","author":"Lavonas","year":"2004","journal-title":"Ann. Emerg. Med."},{"key":"ref_12","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"619","DOI":"10.1067\/mem.2002.129939","article-title":"Crotalidae polyvalent immune Fab (ovine) antivenom is efficacious for envenomations by Southern Pacific rattlesnakes (Crotalus helleri)","volume":"40","author":"Bush","year":"2002","journal-title":"Ann. Emerg. Med."},{"key":"ref_13","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"128","DOI":"10.1016\/j.annemergmed.2010.06.550","article-title":"Short-term outcomes after Fab antivenom therapy for severe crotaline snakebite","volume":"57","author":"Lavonas","year":"2011","journal-title":"Ann. Emerg. Med."}