etic engineering","volume":"15","author":"Wright","year":"1997","journal-title":"Trends Biotechnol."},{"key":"ref_49","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"41","DOI":"10.1038\/538041e","article-title":"Snakebites: Costing recombinant antivenoms","volume":"538","author":"Laustsen","year":"2016","journal-title":"Nature"},{"key":"ref_50","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"151","DOI":"10.1016\/j.toxicon.2018.03.004","article-title":"Pros and cons of different therapeutic antibody formats for recombinant antivenom development","volume":"146","author":"Laustsen","year":"2018","journal-title":"Toxicon"},{"key":"ref_51","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"e2924","DOI":"10.7717\/peerj.2924","article-title":"Exploration of immunoglobulin transcriptomes from mice immunized with three-finger toxins and phospholipases A2 from the Central American coral snake, Micrurus nigrocinctus","volume":"5","author":"Laustsen","year":"2017","journal-title":"PeerJ"},{"key":"ref_52","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Ledsgaard, L., Jenkins, T.P., Davidsen, K., Krause, K.E., Martos-Esteban, A., Engmark, M., R\u00f8rdam Andersen, M., Lund, O., and Laustsen, A.H. (2018). Antibody Cross-Reactivity in Antivenom Research. Toxins, 10.","DOI":"10.3390\/toxins10100393"},{"key":"ref_53","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"195","DOI":"10.1016\/j.toxicon.2018.05.021","article-title":"Toxin-centric development approach for next-generation antivenoms","volume":"150","author":"Laustsen","year":"2018","journal-title":"Toxicon"},{"key":"ref_54","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"2987","DOI":"10.1093\/brain\/awh642","article-title":"Envenoming bites by kraits: The biological basis of treatment-resistant neuromuscular paralysis","volume":"128","author":"Prasarnpun","year":"2005","journal-title":"Brain"},{"key":"ref_55","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Knudsen, C., and Laustsen, A.H. (2018). Recent Advances in Next Generation Snakebite Antivenoms. Trop. Med